Input: {"question": "What is the founding date of the Revolutionary Left Movement?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d00", "start": 0, "end": 206, "text": "Revolutionary Left Movement (Bolivia) The Revolutionary Left Movement - New Majority (Spanish: \"Movimiento de la Izquierda Revolucionaria - Nueva Mayoría\") is a social democratic political party in Bolivia."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d00", "start": 207, "end": 254, "text": "It was a member of the Socialist International."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d00", "start": 255, "end": 435, "text": "The MIR was founded in 1971 by a merger of a left-wing faction of Bolivia's Christian Democratic Party and the radical student wing of the Revolutionary Nationalist Movement (MNR)."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d00", "start": 436, "end": 491, "text": "It has been led from the beginning by Jaime Paz Zamora."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d00", "start": 492, "end": 630, "text": "The MIR was becoming influential in the labor movement and politics during the early 1970s, but it was repressed by the government of Hugo"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d01", "start": 0, "end": 27, "text": "be challenged and removed ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d01", "start": 28, "end": 648, "text": "Find sources : `` Revolutionary Left Movement '' Bolivia – news · newspapers · books · scholar · JSTOR ( August 2008 ) ( Learn how and when to remove this message ) Revolutionary Left Movement – New Majority Movimiento de la Izquierda Revolucionaria – Nueva Mayoría Founded 7 September 1971 Dissolved 2006 Headquarters La Paz Ideology Social democracy Left-wing nationalism Political position Centre-left to left-wing Regional affiliation COPPPAL Politics of Bolivia Political parties Elections The Revolutionary Left Movement – New Majority ( Spanish : Movimiento de la Izquierda Revolucionaria – Nueva Mayoría ; MIR–NM"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d02", "start": 0, "end": 313, "text": "Revolutionary Left Movement (Peru) The Revolutionary Left Movement (in Spanish: \"Movimiento de la Izquierda Revolucionaria\") was a Marxist group founded in Peru in 1962 by Luis de la Puente Uceda and his group \"APRA Rebelde\", a splinter group from the APRA which had rallied the government in the 1950s and 1960s."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d02", "start": 314, "end": 538, "text": "Inspired by the Cuban Revolution and close to a non-aligned position which opposed itself both to the Communist Party of Peru, the Soviet Union and China, the group initiated guerrilla actions against the government in 1965."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d02", "start": 539, "end": 602, "text": "After its leader's death at the end of 1965, the MIR split into"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d03", "start": 0, "end": 75, "text": "'s death at the end of 1965 , the MIR split into three different factions ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d03", "start": 76, "end": 240, "text": "One of them , the MIR-EM , merged with the Revolutionary Socialist Party ( Marxist-Leninist ) in 1982 to create the Movimiento Revolucionario Túpac Amaru ( MRTA ) ."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d03", "start": 241, "end": 368, "text": "The two others factions , MIR-VR and MIR-IV , joined the parliamentary left-wing coalition Izquierda Unida in the early 1980s ."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d03", "start": 369, "end": 537, "text": "( en ) dbo : activeYearsEndYear 1965-01-01 ( xsd : gYear ) dbo : activeYearsStartYear 1962-01-01 ( xsd : gYear ) dbo : colourName Red and black ( en ) dbo : country dbr"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d04", "start": 0, "end": 26, "text": "in Brazil , among others ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d04", "start": 27, "end": 162, "text": "In Peru , the electoral victory in 1962 of Víctor Raúl Haya de la Torre , head of the Peruvian Aprista Party , was annulled by a coup ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d04", "start": 163, "end": 351, "text": "The APRA government program proposed a transformation of the country , betting on agrarian reform to end the servitude regime on the indigenous people that still existed on the haciendas ."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d04", "start": 352, "end": 544, "text": "The Military Junta of 1962 called for new elections for the following year , in which Fernando Belaunde was victorious , who defeated Haya , with a government plan that also proposed to reform"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d05", "start": 0, "end": 86, "text": "then the leader of the socialist cell \"Espartaco\" in Concepción), and Jorge Gutiérrez."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d05", "start": 87, "end": 268, "text": "When this fraction was finally ousted from the Socialist Party (Senator Ampuero) in February 1964, it continued as an independent fraction until they merged in the organization VRM."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d05", "start": 269, "end": 347, "text": "There the young socialists met with Trotskyites, most of them twice their age."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d05", "start": 348, "end": 523, "text": "When MIR was founded on 12 October 1965 at the locals of an anarchist union in Santiago, less than 100 participated, and all the above ideological tendencies were represented."}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d05", "start": 524, "end": 575, "text": "Revolutionary socialists (by Miguel Enríquez and B."}, "D6S6": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d05", "start": 576, "end": 654, "text": "Van Schowen), former communists (represented by the Maoist Cares), Trotskyists"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d06", "start": 0, "end": 42, "text": "Soundings from Southern Peru , 1750–1830 ."}, "D7S2": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d06", "start": 43, "end": 68, "text": "Amsterdam : Aksant 2002 ."}, "D7S3": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d06", "start": 69, "end": 88, "text": "Chambers , Sarah C."}, "D7S4": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d06", "start": 89, "end": 179, "text": "From Subjects to Citizens : Honor , Gender , and Politics in Arequipa , Peru , 1780–1854 ."}, "D7S5": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d06", "start": 180, "end": 221, "text": "University Park : Penn State Press 1999 ."}, "D7S6": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d06", "start": 222, "end": 238, "text": "Charnay , Paul ."}, "D7S7": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d06", "start": 239, "end": 296, "text": "Indian Society in the Valley of Lima , Peru , 1532–1824 ."}, "D7S8": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d06", "start": 297, "end": 351, "text": "Blue Ridge Summit : University Press of America 2001 ."}, "D7S9": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d06", "start": 352, "end": 368, "text": "Dean , Carolyn ."}, "D7S10": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0378-f81fcdb5c963:d06", "start": 369, "end": 447, "text": "Inka Bodies and the Body of Christ : Corpus Christi in Colonial Cuzco , Peru ."}, "D7S11": {"document_number":